    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="efa8b8d1-e062-5829-ac4f-5de053761765" activityNameId="43846edd-0c21-5189-b87b-63b1d4d0ae67" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Disposal, ventilation unit 6700 m3/h, w. heat excanger</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Disposal, ventilation unit 6700 m3/h, w. heat excanger
Disposal of a ventilation unit (air handling unit) with 6700 m3/h nominal air flow rate (at 2 m/s air speed in cross section of air filter or heat exchanger). Reference value of inventory is 1 m3/h air flow. Specific component weight: 0.26 kg/(m3/h), total weight: 0.3 kg/(m3/h), including average components for controls, inverter and electric control cabinet, material for 20 filter replacements (once a year for 20 years lifetime). The air handling unit includes a frame construction, two radial belt drive fans, two multi-leaf damper, heat recovery with average heat exchanger (average of plate, rotary and circuit connected heat exchanger), heating elements, expansion plenum and empty section in supply and extract air. No cooling elements, humidifier, air-mixing plenum and silencer included. The frame construction made of aluminium-profiles, casing made of hot-dip galvanized and powder coated steel sheets insulated with polyurethane foam.;
UUID: 34529094-389f-4202-a09f-8c7138b9726e
Transport to dismantling facilities, machines for handling in sorting plant, electricity demand for sorting plant, final disposal of waste material. Cut-off to recycling for metals.
Location: Specific to the technology mix encountered in sorting plants in Switzerland.
Technology: Disposal to a sorting plant assumed. Metal pieces, copper in cables and electronic devices are recycled, plastic parts are incinerated, inert wastes (e.g. rock wool) are landfilled.
Time period: Amount of material investigated in 2013. Disposal technology mix as used in late 1990ies
Production volume: na
Sampling: Waste-specific calculation based on production input data 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_34529094-389f-4202-a09f-8c7138b9726e.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
